{%- comment -%}
  Shop by Climate hub.

  Copy is from TFS_Shop_by_Climate_Hub_Content_SEO.docx, Part A, used verbatim.
  Part B (technical/on-page SEO) is implemented as the heading hierarchy below
  and the JSON-LD at the foot.

  Three deliberate departures from the document, all because it says so itself
  ("Slugs are best-guess from the keyword sheet tab names. Verify each
  destination slug before publishing"):

  1. Every child slug in the document carries a suffix that does not exist on
     this store — /collections/summer-wear-fragrances, -perfumes and so on. The
     real handles are the bare ones (summer-wear, winter-holiday, …), verified
     against the Admin API. The document's slugs would have shipped ten 404s.
  2. Sections 5 and 6 point at /collections/category, /collections/lifestyle,
     /collections/scent-family, /collections/brands and /collections/shop/*.
     None exist. The equivalents here are /pages/ hubs and bare collection
     handles.
  3. JSON-LD URLs are built from the request rather than hardcoded to
     thefragrancesecrets.com, which does not currently resolve to this store.

  Section 8 (Become a Member) is NOT rendered here: snippets/member-band.liquid
  is already output on every page by the customer-login-cta section, above the
  footer. Repeating it would put the block on the page twice.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign climate_tiles = 'summer-wear|Summer Wear|summer-wear-tile|wb_sunny,winter-holiday|Winter Wear|winter-holiday-tile|ac_unit,spring-bloom|Spring Wear|spring-bloom-hero|local_florist,rainy-day|Rainy Day|rainy-day-tile|rainy,humid-weather|Humid Weather|humid-weather-tile|humidity_high,tropical-climate|Tropical Climate|tropical-climate-tile|forest,desert-climate|Desert Climate|desert-climate-tile|wb_twilight,hot-weather|Hot Weather|hot-weather-hero|thermostat,cold-weather|Cold Weather|cold-weather-hero|severe_cold,dry-weather|Dry Weather|dry-weather-hero|water_drop' | split: ','
-%}

<style>
  /* Four guide cards rather than the three .value-hero assumes. */
  .climate-guide { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .climate-guide .value-card { text-align: left; }
  .climate-guide .cg-tag {
    display: block; margin-top: 14px; font-size: .62rem; letter-spacing: .16em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold-dk);
  }
  /* The document puts FAQ questions at H3. <summary> carries the styling, so
     the heading sits inside it and inherits rather than restyling the row. */
  .faq-q h3 { font: inherit; color: inherit; margin: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 1100px) { .climate-guide { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .climate-guide { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
</style>

<!-- 1 · HERO -->
<section class="page-hero tall">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="breadcrumb">
      <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a>
      <span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">chevron_right</span>
      <span>Shop by Climate</span>
    </div>
    <span class="ph-eyebrow">Match the Weather</span>
    <h1 class="ph-title">Shop by <em>Climate</em></h1>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 2 · COLLECTION INTRODUCTION -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 class="sec-title">Shop Perfume by Weather and Season in the UAE</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="legal-prose">
      <p>The right fragrance can make all the difference when temperatures change. The Fragrance Secrets makes it easier to shop perfumes based on the weather you actually experience in the UAE, from hot and humid summer days to cooler winter evenings, dry desert weather, and refreshing rainy afternoons. Instead of browsing through hundreds of fragrances, explore curated collections designed around different weather conditions and seasonal preferences. Discover fresh scents for the heat, richer fragrances for cooler days, and versatile options that perform beautifully throughout the year. Explore every weather-based collection and build a fragrance wardrobe suited to the UAE climate.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 3 · EXPLORE CLIMATE COLLECTIONS -->
<section class="section alt">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="label">Explore Climate Collections</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Every Edit, <em>One Kind of Weather</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">Every edit is curated for a specific type of weather. Choose the one that fits your day and discover fragrances suited to it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hub-grid four fade-up">
      {%- for tile in climate_tiles -%}
        {%- assign parts = tile | split: '|' -%}
        {%- assign handle = parts[0] -%}
        {%- assign label = parts[1] -%}
        {%- assign img = parts[2] -%}
        {%- assign icon = parts[3] -%}
        {%- assign coll = collections[handle] -%}
        <a class="hub-tile" href="{{ coll.url | default: '/collections/all' }}">
          <img src="{{ img | append: '.webp' | asset_url }}"
               srcset="{{ img | append: '-sm.webp' | asset_url }} 600w, {{ img | append: '.webp' | asset_url }} 1200w"
               sizes="(max-width: 600px) 92vw, (max-width: 1100px) 46vw, 23vw"
               alt="{{ label }} perfume edit UAE" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800">
          <div class="hub-body">
            <span class="hub-ic"><span class="mi mi-f" aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--gold-lt)">{{ icon }}</span></span>
            <h3>{{ label }}</h3>
            <span class="hub-go">Explore <span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">arrow_forward</span></span>
          </div>
        </a>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 4 · HOW TO SHOP BY CLIMATE -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="label">How to Shop by Climate</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Let the Weather <em>Choose for You</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">Shopping by climate takes the guesswork out of choosing a scent that lasts. Instead of browsing thousands of options, you start with the weather and let it guide you. Here is how to make the most of the climate edits.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="value-hero climate-guide fade-up">
      <div class="value-card">
        <span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">thermostat</span>
        <h3>Read the Temperature</h3>
        <p>Heat lifts a fragrance and makes it project more, while cold holds it close to the skin. Start with how hot or cool your day is, and let that guide how strong a scent you reach for.</p>
        <span class="cg-tag">Explore · Hot · Warm · Cool · Cold</span>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card">
        <span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">humidity_high</span>
        <h3>Mind the Humidity</h3>
        <p>Humid air makes rich scents feel heavier and can turn them sharp. On sticky days, lighter fresh and citrus fragrances stay clean, while in dry air deeper scents bloom without feeling overwhelming.</p>
        <span class="cg-tag">Best for · Humid · Dry · Tropical</span>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card">
        <span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">calendar_month</span>
        <h3>Match the Season</h3>
        <p>Summer suits fresh, aquatic and citrus notes. Winter is made for oud, amber and spice. Spring and cooler months sit in between, where soft florals and light woods feel just right.</p>
        <span class="cg-tag">Best for · Summer · Winter · Spring · Rainy</span>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card">
        <span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">autorenew</span>
        <h3>Build a Seasonal Rotation</h3>
        <p>Most people need more than one signature. Shopping by climate helps you build a small rotation, a fresh scent for the heat, a warm one for cooler months, and something easy for in between.</p>
        <span class="cg-tag">Best for · Everyday · Seasonal · Signature</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 5 · EXPLORE MORE FRAGRANCE COLLECTIONS -->
